 "final_summary": "The root cause was a race condition in the `next()` method of `TicketSequence` where multiple threads could read the same value of `_next` before it was incremented, leading to duplicate ticket numbers. The fix ensures atomicity by holding the lock during both the read and increment operations, preventing concurrent access and guaranteeing unique ticket numbers under load.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/sequence.py b/tracker/sequence.py\nindex f76c315..9f2750c 100644\n--- a/tracker/sequence.py\n+++ b/tracker/sequence.py\n@@ -15,9 +15,8 @@ class TicketSequence:\n     def next(self):\n         with self._lock:\n             current = self._next\n-        self._store(current + 1)\n-        self.issued.append(current)\n+            self._next = current + 1\n+            self.issued.append(current)\n         return current\n-\n     def peek(self):\n         return self._next\n",
